WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.434
-We have something in common.
We both --

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.103
-Just one thing.
-Only one thing.

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:05.538
[ Laughter ]
-Just one.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.440
-I know. Pick one of the many
things we do have in common.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.376
We both drive trucks.
-When did you get a truck?

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.912
-I got a truck --
I got a Ford F-150.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.148
I've had it now
probably 10 years now.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.682
-What?
-Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:18.717
I have a picture.
This is my --

00:00:18.717 --> 00:00:20.252
This is my Ford --
This things is unbelievable.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:22.354
-You drive a truck?
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:23.856
I like it.
It's like blue

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.625
and, like, kind of khaki pants.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.759
It looks like
it works at Best Buy.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.094
-So, wait -- khakis.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.262
It looks like
it works at Best Buy.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.297
-Wait. Do you name --
Did you name your truck?

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.631
-You know,
I was gonna name it...

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:33.966
-What?
-...but I ended up not doing it.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.869
Yeah, I didn't name it.
-That's rude.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.336
-Let me see --
-I have a truck.

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:39.705
I have a truck.
Yours is really cute.

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:41.140
[ Laughter ]
This is a --

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.376
This is a --
This is a real truck.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.045
This is an F-250.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.714
-F-250?
-Yes.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:48.848
-Let me see that thing.
-But your --

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.283
But your little F-150
looks adorable.

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.253
Did it come
with a remote control?

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.955
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.723
-What do you do with it?
That's gin--

00:00:57.723 --> 00:00:59.659
-No. I -- It is ridiculous,
because here's the thing.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:03.329
I had it at my ranch in Montana,
and it made sense there.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.598
You know, use it for things.
But then I took it

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.634
for a while to L.A., and --
But I will say,

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.771
what reminds me of your truck
is, whenever I pulled up

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.974
at "The Voice," Blake has a cute
little truck like you, too.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.676
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.845
I pulled up next to his,
and he's, like, giant,

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:21.614
and his is, like, smaller.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.049
-It was tiny.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.617
-Yeah, and I'm like 5'3 1/2",
and I'm like, I'm getting out...

00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:26.752
-Yeah.
[ imitates truck horn ]

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.121
-Anyway, I felt powerful.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.256
Her name is Betty White,
so, yeah.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.590
[ Laughter ]
-Betty White.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.426
That's a great one, by the way.
-Her name is Betty.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.894
Why did you originally
get a truck?

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:39.131
-I wanted -- I wanted to bring
pumpkins to my house from --

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:42.134
[ Laughter ]
When it's, uh --

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:44.636
It was pumpkin season,
so there was, like, pumpkins.

00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:47.139
I didn't want to put pumpkins
in a car, in a thing,

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.742
so I got a truck.
-Got some first-world problems.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.711
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.446
-I've only use it
like once a year.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.448
-I guess I should get a Hummer
because I need pumpkins.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.483
[ Laughter ]
That's awesome.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.718
-I had to transport
the pumpkins.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.519
-That's me, too.
I got it for Lowe's.

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:02.288
-Yeah, understood.
See?

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.390
We have more things in common.
-They're so comfortable.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.459
I want to take a road trip
just so I can be in it.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.960
-Me too.
I love a good sound system.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.629
-Yes.
-The whole thing is great.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:10.763
I want to talk about
"The Voice."

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.832
-Yes.
-I hear you guys are coming back

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.034
with brand-new judge...
-Ariana.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.502
-...Ariana Grande.
-Yeah!

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:17.970
It's so good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.872
Yeah.
-How are you guys?

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:21.140
Are you gelling?
Are you bonding?

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.342
-We're -- Are you gellin'?
I'm gellin'.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:25.044
The commercial.
Anyway...

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.212
No, I love her.
We'd actually run into

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:29.315
each other a couple times
before, but not really, like,

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.916
you know, been able to,
like, talk.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:33.652
And she's so funny.
-She is funny.

00:02:33.652 --> 00:02:35.354
-Like, very witty.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:37.189
-Like, in the beginning,
even, like, behind the scenes,

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:39.892
like, she wasn't, like,
using a lot of her material

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.293
she could've used out there,
and then I feel like

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:42.628
slowly towards the knockouts --

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.197
Like, we've already taped
everything up to the lives,

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.598
and she's hysterical.
Like, very witty.

00:02:46.598 --> 00:02:48.868
And very -- We've never
had a coach like her.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.570
I've only been there
for eight seasons but, like,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.372
in all my seasons,
I've never heard a coach

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.973
talk about vocal health as much.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.242
And I'm like, "I guess we should
have mentioned that."

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.877
[ Laughter ]
-We are called "The Voice."

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.679
-We're all, like, vocalists.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.815
Like, no one's ever mentioned
it, and she's really into it.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:03.950
So, it's cool.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.451
And everybody vibes so well.
It's good.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.653
-How is it
to film with a live audience?

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:08.955
-Great!
So that's -- Oh, my God.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.423
This is funny.
So, we all have to --

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.724
Now that we're back
with a live audience --

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.492
we haven't been, I feel like,
in a couple seasons,

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:16.029
two or three --
and when we walk out,

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.496
they have the coaches
walk out separately.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:18.765
-Yeah.
-Like, they have all us walk out

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.200
separately and like,
"You know, and John Legend,"

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.468
and then we get all of us
or whatever.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.103
Did you like that?
That's dumb.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.505
Anyway...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.507
That was a poor example.
But anyway.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.541
So we're walking out, and I go
out and they're like, "Yay!"

00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:32.044
And then John goes out, "Yay,"
and then Ariana goes out,

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:34.980
and it's literally like BTS
has entered the building.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.150
Like, they lose their minds.
-Yeah.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.219
-And then,
Blake has to follow it.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:41.821
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.289
Because they're like --
'Cause they --

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.791
He comes out, and they're like
clapping like they were.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:49.395
But it was like, "Mur mur mur."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.430
[ Sad tuba plays ]
I know Blake was like,

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.766
"Could I go before Ariana?
Like, this is embarrassing."

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.201
-"I don't want to follow that."
-Yeah.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.769
They literally lost their minds.
-Yeah.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.003
-She's -- yeah, yeah.
-It's exciting.

00:03:58.003 --> 00:03:59.372
It's gonna be fun to watch.
-Yeah.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.773
-Thank you so much, again,
for coming back to our show.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.141
-And I'm so sorry that I
screwed up all the interview.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.909
[ Cheers and applause ]
-And for being here in studio.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:06.045
We don't need this.
You're the greatest.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.614
-Yeah.
-Kelly Clarkson, everybody!

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.315
-This is the truck.
-The new season

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:13.052
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"
premieres September 13th,

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.553
and the new season
of "The Voice"

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.055
returns September 20th.

